WEBVTT

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.100
Good morning.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.940
Good morning!

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.940
Huh? Could that be...

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.030
Linca-san?

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.810
Why, isn't it Escha?

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.600
Good morning.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.710
Speaking of which, why are you here?

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.010
Come on.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:28.000
I'm officially a member of the R&D department now.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.670
Oh, I see.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.900
You started while I was away on my assignment.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:37.150
So you must be the other alchemist, Logy, right?

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.250
Yes. It's a pleasure.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.180
Linca-san is a swordswoman working for the R&D department,

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.040
and she's so strong that the Combat Department asks her to go on expedition missions with them!

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.750
So that's why she carries such a big sword with her.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:53.900
I'm going on another mission today, so I'm here to fill up.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.530
What do you mean, "fill up"?!

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.300
It's just like you to take me by surprise, Marion.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.160
I couldn't sense you at all!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.010
Aren't those the rations for your mission?!

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.920
Why are you eating them now?

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.160
I'm sorry!

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.640
That's dangerous!

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.420
Geez! You're always like this!

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.780
The two of them are such good friends.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.970
You think so?

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.980
So what is it that you wanted to show me?

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:02.310
It just got here this morning, and I don't really know much about it...

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.490
What do you think?

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:09.110
It's an Imbuing Table!

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:10.290
Imbuing Table?

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:13.830
Unlike an alchemical cauldron,

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:17.490
this device is made to draw the ingredients' power out.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.880
You can use it to strengthen weapons and equipment.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.990
This will work just fine.

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.140
Thank you, Manager.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.060
Oh yeah, Linca-san,

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.600
since you already ate your food,

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:34.020
take this instead.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.570
This much?

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.300
Thank you!

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.990
I'll definitely return the favour.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.880
Now then, I'll take my leave.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.200
Be safe!

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.450
Okay, it's time we talk about work.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:56.710
I want you two to resupply a village to the north of Colseit.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:58.640
Resupply, is it?

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:04.730
From what the villagers told us, the village lake is becoming stagnate since less water is flowing from upstream.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:07.130
They're worried about running out of drinking water.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:09.600
So we need to deliver water via balloon, right?

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.460
That's right.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.560
Please work together and help the village out.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.100
Understood.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.440
Logy-san, let's go see Onii-chan right away!

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.580
Um, this is...

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.620
Sadly, it's exactly as you see.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:35.170
Can't we inflate it?

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.590
There's a hole in it.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.420
This will be difficult without the balloon.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:47.180
If you could persuade Solle to let us get a new one, you'd be able to use it right away.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.760
I-I can't do that.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.280
I guessed as much.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:54.230
Even I can't persuade him, even though we started working at the same time.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:57.670
Well, we'll be able to use it again once we fix it.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:59.050
Let's get started, Awin.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:04:59.730
Understood.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.990
I guess we'll just have to wait until it's fixed.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.190
If we can't go by air, we'll just go by land.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.530
Let's get ourselves a wagon!

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.160
We don't have the budget for that.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:17.470
Awin just requested funds to repair the balloon.

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:21.890
I am sorry for leaving you dry despite the urgency, but please find another way.

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:23.550
Yes.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.050
I guess we'll just have to wait until it's fixed.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:32.230
But if that's the case, the villagers may run out of water.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:35.020
I want to help them right away!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.940
Oh yeah! I should visit the archives!

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:38.650
What for?

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:43.370
To see if there are any recipes.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:50.780
Say, for ways to make water lighter,
medicines that'll strengthen our muscles,

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:55.630
a flying carpet, or a door that'll take us anywhere instantly!

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.380
There's no such things.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.670
You should face reality.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:00.380
There are!

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:04.530
There's definitely something that we can do!

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.470
That's because we're alchemists!

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:12.490
We have the ability to help others in need.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:15.980
Let's work hard to help everyone, okay?

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:20.440
Even though I said that,

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:23.130
it's not like we'd find a way so soon.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.400
Of course.

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:28.860
Onii-san, Onee-san, are the two of you worried about something?

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.960
In that case, please visit Katla's Shoppe!

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.620
Whether famous or new, we have all sorts of things here!

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.870
Was there a shop here?

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.260
I'm opening it here starting today.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.670
I got no visitors at my last spot.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.910
That's quite a variety.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:48.050
This looks like it can be used for synthesis.

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:51.370
You sure have a fine taste, Sir!

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:53.510
So, what are you going to do with that kind of thing?

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.320
Did you just say "that kind of"?

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:58.070
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:59.920
That was just a slip of tongue.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.770
What you are looking at is quite rare, after all.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:05.650
We're alchemists working for the branch just over there.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:10.200
My! You two are such beauties, just as your job implies!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.410
You have no idea what an alchemist is, do you?

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:17.170
You can tell me more about that as we get to know each other.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.980
I look forward to your continued business.

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:23.250
You sure get carried away.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.340
This book...

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:35.050
This is it!

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.420
Katla-chan, is it?

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:39.600
I'll take this book!

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:50.360
So what's inside?

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:51.970
Here.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.780
Purify Bottle?

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:01.760
It seems the liquid from the bottle will purify whatever water it comes into contact with.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:03.610
So a medicine like this exists?

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:05.380
But it must be difficult to make?

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.300
Let's see...

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:14.220
Looks like we'll need Zettel, Metal, Supplement, and something called Bitter Leaf for ingredients?

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.090
Bitter Leaf?

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.680
I've never heard of that ingredient before.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.420
This is also the first time I've run across it.

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:20.760
Where can we get it?

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.710
Okay, enough about work.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:24.690
Why so much?

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:27.830
Duke's meals are always so hearty.

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:30.210
Logy, if you're a man, chow down.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:31.280
No need to hold back.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.420
Even if you say that...

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:36.650
This is delicious!

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:38.640
I might actually be able to finish this.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.600
Isn't it?

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.750
So what's this about Bitter Leaf, Escha-chan?

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:49.210
Duke-san, you've heard of it?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.850
Of course.

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:53.650
I also used to be a member of the Colseit Branch's Combat Department.

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:55.680
I know just about everything around here.

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:59.220
You're awesome, Duke-san!

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:04.850
If it's Bitter Leaf that you want, you can find some in the ruins just north of the village.

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:08.320
Though both monsters and beasts lurk at the ruins,

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:10.490
as well as thieves sometimes too.

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:12.360
It's too dangerous for you.

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:15.400
There's Bitter Leaf here.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:19.090
It takes a day and a half to get to the village from Colseit.

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:23.250
If we count the time it takes to get to the ruins, we should get there the day after tomorrow.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.080
You really want to go?

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.000
It's dangerous.

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:27.340
I'm going.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:30.840
We need this ingredient to help the villagers.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.790
Got it.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:36.590
Let's go.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:37.760
I'll protect you, Escha.

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:39.940
Logy-san!

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:51.070
Oh yeah! Let's make that too.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:04.870
Awesome! It's done!

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:11.030
We just need to add the Bitter Leaf now.

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:14.960
Good morning, Escha-chan.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.180
Good morning, Marion-san.

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:18.720
What's all that?

00:10:19.030 --> 00:10:21.130
Logy-kun asked me to get this.

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:22.830
Logy-san did?

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:26.480
I figured that if they're running out of water, they'd probably be out of food too.

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:30.350
Are we delivering all this to the villagers?

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:32.450
Why are you spacing out now?

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:33.610
Let's get ready.

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:36.070
Okay!

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:46.000
Let's go, Logy-san!

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:09.890
I wonder if this can be used for synthesis.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:11.850
I'll take some.

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:15.750
This too!

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:17.060
This looks so pretty!

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:19.280
It must be a very rare ingredient!

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.740
It doesn't feel like she's out here for work.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:26.040
Logy-san, if you find anything, be sure to pick some up too!

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:29.000
Even if you say so...

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:36.380
I never really went outside to gather ingredients when I was at Central.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.590
I wonder if there's a use for this kind of flower.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:47.900
Let's camp here for the night.

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:56.050
So you learned swordsmanship at Central too, Logy-san?

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:59.400
Yeah, but it's just for exercise and fun.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:02.280
When I was there, I locked myself in the lab.

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:06.660
So you had something you were fascinated with.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:09.610
Yeah.

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:38.190
Good morning!

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:40.880
Today's the day, Logy-san!

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:43.320
Let's find some Bitter Leaf!

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.200
Yeah.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.970
This place is in pretty bad shape.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:11.670
D-Did you hear that noise just now?

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:12.790
Don't let your guard down.

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:14.100
We don't know what's going to come at us.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:18.060
I hope we can find some today.

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:39.440
It's probably better if we split up to find it.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:42.000
Logy-san, I'll look in that direction.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.330
Don't go too far.

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:45.270
Okay.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:51.690
This isn't it.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:53.960
Either is this.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:13:59.550
This isn't it, huh?

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:03.190
It doesn't look like there's any over here either.

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.360
Escha, want to go further inside?

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:08.700
Escha?

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.620
Where did she go?

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:18.580
It doesn't look like there's anything like it here.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:25.610
What's this?

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:27.110
I've never seen this flower before!

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:28.380
I wonder if I can use it.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:32.390
Don't touch that!

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.310
Escha!

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:42.210
There she is!

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:49.150
What is she doing to Escha?

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:52.240
Hey! What do you think you're doing?!

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:01.520
Hey! What are you doing to my friend?!

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:02.630
What's with that all of a sudden?!

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:05.370
Nio's trying to help that girl.

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:06.590
Can't you tell just by looking?

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:08.850
Help?

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:17.470
How is it?

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.430
The paralysis is gone!

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:27.540
Thank goodness.

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:28.860
You should be fine now.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:30.820
Thank you.

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:33.280
I didn't know that flower was poisonous.

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:35.370
So that's what was going on.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.680
Sorry for causing such a commotion.

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:40.650
I don't know what would have happened if she wasn't here.

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:42.290
Um, what's your name?

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:45.190
I'm Nio, a travelling apothecary.

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:47.090
She also travels with me.

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:52.300
I'm the Great Mage Wilbell voll-Erslied.

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:53.890
Great Mage?

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.340
Forget about that!

00:15:56.340 --> 00:15:57.760
My being a mage is a secret!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.720
I'm Escha Malier.

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:03.440
Logix Fiscario.

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:04.770
Just Logy is fine.

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:08.980
We're alchemists working for the Colseit Branch's R&D Department.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:11.500
Branch... so that means...?

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:15.320
What business do government officials such as yourselves have out here?

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:18.700
We came to the ruins for gathering.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:20.200
Gathering?

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:24.080
It's called Bitter Leaf. Have you seen it?

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:28.180
We have to find this today.

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:28.920
Today?

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:33.550
We need to finish this medicine to help the villagers.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:37.930
Doesn't look like they're looking for her.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:40.720
Yeah, looks like they are very dignified alchemists.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.820
Now that we've come to an understanding, we don't mind helping you.

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:48.570
If you're looking for where the Bitter Leaves are, I can take you there.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.110
Really?

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:51.740
Thank you!

00:16:57.430 --> 00:17:00.790
You can find those leaves in the ruins' darker spots.

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:16.690
What's this?

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:17.840
A painting of a girl?

00:17:21.320 --> 00:17:22.950
That's weird.

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:25.270
I can't find any.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.270
I'm sorry, Escha-chan. You two are in a hurry after all.

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:28.570
That's okay.

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:30.630
I haven't given up yet.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:32.900
Let's do our best until we find it!

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:37.400
They're just like each other.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:39.200
She's also a very hardworking person.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:40.130
Yeah.

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:43.650
She always does her best for somebody else, and is very earnest.

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:44.570
Hey!

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.160
Come over here!

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:52.090
Is that...?

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.050
It's Bitter Leaf!

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:57.680
But it's on top of the wall...

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.550
Logy-san?

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:08.330
I think I can do it.

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.360
You can't climb it!

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:17.320
It's dangerous, Logy-san!

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.870
I'll be fine.

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:22.220
You're trying your best to help the villagers.

00:18:22.220 --> 00:18:26.080
It's my job to help you out.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:28.040
Logy-san.

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:32.710
I guess all male alchemists are morons.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:36.170
It's so wonderful that he's doing his best for a girl.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:48.520
Okay.

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:49.230
I got it, Escha!

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:55.280
Wind, blow!

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.490
What the?

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:06.240
Is this... magic?

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:09.960
You're really a mage, Wilbell-san?

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:13.710
I'm only showing it to you two since you're so interesting.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:15.130
Don't tell anyone.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.930
Yes! Thank you!

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:20.260
Thank you very much, Wilbell-san!

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:23.110
Come on, if you're so happy, it makes me feel embarrassed!

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:25.150
This is a piece of cake...

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:26.140
Huh?

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:29.910
Whoops.

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:31.690
Logy-san!

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:36.130
Thank goodness you're okay!

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:37.940
What are you crying for?

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:39.470
That's because...!

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:40.650
Here.

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:43.990
We aren't done yet, right?

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:46.700
Yes!

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:17.950
I wonder what that is.

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.220
Who knows?

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:22.530
I hope this goes well.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.920
It didn't work?

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:03.320
Success!

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:06.700
I can't believe it'd be so clean...

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:12.840
Thank you!

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:14.620
Thank you!

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:17.830
I'm glad everything worked out.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:19.130
That's amazing.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:22.550
She managed to do all that herself.

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:26.260
Logy-san!

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:29.970
You're amazing, Escha.

00:21:54.740 --> 00:21:56.420
Stay away.
